WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.180
Two clear solutions stand side by side:
lead nitrate and potassium iodide.

2
00:00:06.180 --> 00:00:10.480
When they meet, a yellow solid
forms and clouds the mixture.

3
00:00:10.480 --> 00:00:12.620
Chemists call it a precipitate.

4
00:00:12.620 --> 00:00:14.520
It is lead iodide.

5
00:00:14.520 --> 00:00:17.340
Each solution held its own particles.

6
00:00:17.340 --> 00:00:22.920
So when two clear solutions make a cloudy
solid, which particles actually react?

7
00:00:22.920 --> 00:00:27.920
In this mission, you'll sort reactions
into three kinds: acid–base,

8
00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:33.640
redox and precipitation, by following
protons, electrons or a new solid.

9
00:00:33.640 --> 00:00:38.920
Then you'll write one reaction in three
different ways, and see what each way shows.

10
00:00:38.920 --> 00:00:44.360
Your mission: find out which particles really
react when two solutions make a solid.